    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0984" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg888"/>

                <head>No. 401.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christiancy to Mr.
                    Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 23, 1879</date>.
                        (Received August 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 39.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copy of my
                    letter of this date to Mr. Merriam, our consul at Iquique, together with an
                    extract of the letter of the consul to me of July 10 (his No. 38), in reference
                    to the right of the Chilian fleet to prevent the shipping of nitrates from
                    Pisagua.</p>
                <p>As to the circumstances going to show whether the blockade of Iquique had been
                    raised, you will find them stated with substantial accuracy in my dispatch No.
                    34 (July 15). * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d432-a1.xml" xpointer="d432-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d432-a2.xml" xpointer="d432-a2"/>
